  "response_text": "If we don\u2019t set the PSP to point to the new thread\u2019s stack, the CPU will try to load registers from the wrong memory location during context switching. Since the default stack pointer (MSP) is being used by the main program, using it for a thread would cause a conflict or access invalid memory, resulting in a hard fault. By switching to the PSP, we isolate the thread\u2019s execution and give it its own dedicated stack space.\\n",
